---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import data from '../../data/content.json';
const {themes} = data;
---
<Shell title="Theme library"><a class="back-link" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the puzzle</a><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">Theme library</span> <h1>Read every thread</h1> <p>Thirty sets of three passages. Solve a thread in Ayah Threads first, then come back to read its theme and the commentary.</p></section><section class="panel bottom-gap"><div class="panel-body"><div class="filters"><label class="field">Area<select id="category"><option value="">All areas</option>{['Character','Community','Reflection','Worship'].map(g=><option>{g}</option>)}</select></label> <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="saved-only"/>Saved only</label></div> <p class="micro top-gap" id="solved-count" aria-live="polite">0 of {themes.length} themes solved</p><p class="micro" id="shown-count" role="status">{themes.length} of {themes.length} threads shown</p></div></section><noscript><div class="noscript">Saving and solved state need JavaScript. Every thread page below can still be read, with its theme behind a closed spoiler.</div></noscript><div class="card-grid">{themes.map(t=><><article class="panel activity-card" data-item-id={t.id} data-category={t.category}><span class="eyebrow">{t.category}</span> <span class="pill solved-pill" hidden>Solved</span><h2><a href={`/themes/${t.id}/`}>{t.title}</a></h2> <p class="micro" data-theme-name hidden></p> <p>Quran {t.refs.join(', ')}</p> <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/themes/${t.id}/`}>Read the passages <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> <button class="button secondary" type="button" data-save={t.id} aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div></article>{' '}</>)}</div> <div id="empty" class="empty" hidden><h2>No threads match</h2> <p>Change the area, or turn off Saved only.</p></div></Shell>
<script>import '../../lib/themes';</script>
<style>.solved-pill[hidden],[data-theme-name][hidden]{display:none}.solved-pill{align-self:start}</style>
